<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carlos Prío Socarrás</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1903">1903</a>–<a href="/years/1977">1977</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carlos Prío Socarrás was a Cuban politician of the Auténtico Party who was elected president in 1948. His government created the National Bank of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> but was widely seen as corrupt and plagued by political gang violence. He was overthrown by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fulgencio-batista">Fulgencio Batista</a>'s coup of 10 March 1952, shortly before new elections, and later backed the opposition from exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carlos-prio-socarras.jpg" alt="Carlos Prío Socarrás" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Otero, Juan Joaquin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carlos_Prio_Socarras_of_Cuba.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
